# Deploy & operate an Autopoet brain

The payoff of the whole stack: help a human stand up an autonomous worker — an **Autopoet brain** — in the
cloud, and know how it thinks. This is the "operate Autopoet" half of the external experience.

**When to use:** a user wants a headless agent running in their cloud org — provisioning it, addressing
it, or wiring its LLM.

## What a "brain" is
A headless Autopoet — the same agent as the desktop app, minus the GUI + local voice/ML (those are
desktop-only; the cloud brain is stubbed there). It ships as the `AUTOPOET_IMAGE` (`registry.fly.io/
autopoet:v1`), provisioned as a per-tenant Fly machine in the org's Fly org (`FLY_ORG_SLUG`, authed with
`FLY_ORG_TOKEN`). It serves its control surface on the machine's public port; the nexus runs alongside it.

## Standing one up
- `work cloud provision` (or `POST /api/cloud/provision`) — provisions / rolls this org's brain machine.
  `work cloud machine` inspects state + image; `work cloud down` tears it down. **Provisioning is billable
  — flag it to the human.**
- Requires the org's provisioning secrets in the store: `FLY_ORG_TOKEN`, `FLY_ORG_SLUG`, `AUTOPOET_IMAGE`.
  A fresh machine boots healthy only with a `WB_SESSION_SECRET` — the provisioner injects one per machine.

## How it thinks — LLM through OUR gateway
Every brain routes its LLM through the **Cloudflare AI Gateway**: `Nexus.Llm` auto-detects `CF_AIG_URL` +
`CF_AIG_TOKEN` (injected into the machine) and sends completions through the gateway — metered, no
per-tenant provider keys. A brain with no gateway creds is inert; a brain with them thinks + is billed.

## The discipline
- **Escalate the billable/irreversible** — provision + teardown cost money; get a human OK.
- **Verify it's alive** — after provisioning, confirm the machine is `started` + health-passing before
  reporting success; a booted-but-crashing brain is not a deploy.
